WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:01.804
(cat meowing)

00:00:01.804 --> 00:00:02.884
- [Shaun] A lot of people

00:00:02.884 --> 00:00:03.870
see a cat up in a tree,

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:04.703
they're just like,

00:00:04.703 --> 00:00:06.669
"Oh, yeah, that thing'll get
down here in a couple days."

00:00:06.669 --> 00:00:09.498
- [Tom] Hi sweetie, how
long you been in this tree?

00:00:09.498 --> 00:00:11.561
But what they don't realize is that

00:00:11.561 --> 00:00:13.813
sometimes they don't.

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:16.113
I'm Shaun Sears.

00:00:16.113 --> 00:00:19.158
- And I'm Tom Otto with Canopy Cat Rescue.

00:00:19.158 --> 00:00:21.449
- And we rescue cats that
get stuck up in trees.

00:00:21.449 --> 00:00:24.032
(upbeat music)

00:00:27.305 --> 00:00:28.221
(cat meowing)

00:00:28.221 --> 00:00:30.058
- [Shaun] There you go, oh, let go.

00:00:30.058 --> 00:00:32.111
- Cats get stuck in trees a lot.

00:00:32.111 --> 00:00:33.591
- We've been rescuing

00:00:33.591 --> 00:00:34.870
since about 2008.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:36.022
- [Shaun] I'm getting ya.

00:00:36.022 --> 00:00:39.728
We probably do more cat rescues
than anybody in the world.

00:00:39.728 --> 00:00:40.624
- I got you.

00:00:40.624 --> 00:00:41.968
- We range from about

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:45.085
375 to 400 rescues every year.

00:00:45.085 --> 00:00:47.174
- [Tom] It's okay.

00:00:47.174 --> 00:00:48.558
- There's a lot of people

00:00:48.558 --> 00:00:50.111
that can't afford to pay

00:00:50.111 --> 00:00:51.867
your normal arborist
five, six, 700 dollars

00:00:51.867 --> 00:00:53.121
to rescue a cat.

00:00:53.121 --> 00:00:55.104
Both Tom and I really love cats.

00:00:55.104 --> 00:00:58.865
- [Tom] He's a total sweetie, ginger boy.

00:00:58.865 --> 00:01:00.506
- We'll come out and rescue

00:01:00.506 --> 00:01:01.745
somebody's cat for free.

00:01:01.745 --> 00:01:02.879
- [Tom] Hi sweetie.

00:01:02.879 --> 00:01:03.950
(phone ringing)

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:04.783
- Alright.

00:01:04.783 --> 00:01:06.958
Canopy Cat Rescue, this is Shaun.

00:01:06.958 --> 00:01:08.173
- [Man] Yeah, it's our cat.

00:01:08.173 --> 00:01:09.276
She's climbed up

00:01:09.276 --> 00:01:11.712
and she's been up there
for three or four hours

00:01:11.712 --> 00:01:13.188
and it just doesn't look like

00:01:13.188 --> 00:01:14.069
she's gonna figure this out.

00:01:14.069 --> 00:01:15.718
- Well, I think we'll be there in

00:01:15.718 --> 00:01:17.374
about 45 minutes or so.

00:01:17.374 --> 00:01:20.768
- [Tom] Climbing trees
is inherently risky.

00:01:20.768 --> 00:01:23.944
- Our average tree
height is a hundred feet.

00:01:23.944 --> 00:01:26.276
Sometimes they're a lot taller.

00:01:26.276 --> 00:01:27.733
- [Shaun] We sort of suss out

00:01:27.733 --> 00:01:29.978
how the cat's doing as
we're getting close.

00:01:29.978 --> 00:01:31.128
- [Tom] Hi.

00:01:31.128 --> 00:01:34.198
- [Shaun] And then hopefully
we can proceed with the rescue.

00:01:34.198 --> 00:01:36.094
- [Tom] You never want to stay.

00:01:36.094 --> 00:01:37.435
How's that sound?

00:01:37.435 --> 00:01:39.935
(cat meowing)

00:01:41.182 --> 00:01:42.948
- [Woman] Wow!

00:01:42.948 --> 00:01:44.824
Good whew.

00:01:44.824 --> 00:01:46.899
- [Shaun] The look that we get

00:01:46.899 --> 00:01:48.835
from the cat owner's face when we

00:01:48.835 --> 00:01:50.529
hand 'em their cat back

00:01:50.529 --> 00:01:53.805
is just this overwhelming sense of relief.

00:01:53.805 --> 00:01:56.488
- [Tom] Are you happy to have him back?

00:01:56.488 --> 00:01:57.453
He's, I know.

00:01:57.453 --> 00:01:59.567
- You have no idea .

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:02.397
- [Shaun] We love doing
this and we're gonna do it

00:02:02.397 --> 00:02:03.837
for as long as we can.

00:02:03.837 --> 00:02:06.197
You said you got a cat stuck in a tree?

00:02:06.197 --> 00:02:07.030
- Bella!

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:09.457
- We don't really
consider ourselves heroes,

00:02:09.457 --> 00:02:10.688
but we do like to think of ourselves

00:02:10.688 --> 00:02:12.184
as just two guys that are out there

00:02:12.184 --> 00:02:14.934
restoring the faith in humanity.

